  "answer": "Both requests have been made before, and the Terminal team has declined the width one. Terminal#9218 and #18937 asked for a configurable scrollbar width. The maintainers said they would rather not add a Terminal-only setting that makes it differ from Windows, and neither request was implemented. Terminal#3454 and #12395 cover the scrollbar being too narrow to grab and are the closest places to add your accessibility case. Terminal#3454 also says the Terminal can't easily keep the scrollbar expanded unless it re-templates the control.\n\nFor keeping the scrollbar always visible, terminal#14589 says a scrollbar visibility option of \"Always\" was added in Terminal 1.17. Set it under Settings > [Profile or Defaults] > Appearance > Scrollbar visibility. If you only see Visible and Hidden, update Terminal. A related ticket (#9346) says the Windows setting 'Automatically hide scroll bars in Windows' (under Accessibility > Visual effects) also affects Terminal's scrollbar, and Terminal may need a restart to pick up a change. I did not find a ticket confirming that this keeps the bar expanded at full width. You can comment on #9218 or #3454 to explain the accessibility need and ask for a wider bar."
 },
